{"id":5,"role":"User","content":"## Project: YangMills — Lean 4 formalization of Yang-Mills mass gap\n\nYou are continuing work on closing `transferMatrixPositivity_axiom` (the only achievable axiom reduction; would reduce axiom count 6→5). The project is at `C:\\github\\YangMills`, Lean 4 / Mathlib, builds clean with `lake build` (2972 jobs, 0 errors).\n\n## Current state (verified this session)\n\n**Build status:** `lake build` succeeds cleanly (2972 jobs). `git status` shows uncommitted modifications to README.md, docs/gap_analysis.md, Overview.lean, LatticeMeasure.lean, PeterWeyl.lean, ReflectionPositivity.lean, TransferMatrix.lean, plus untracked docs/transfer_matrix_positivity_design.md. These are all from prior sessions and are in a consistent, building state.\n\n**Axiom count: 6** (verified in README). The six axioms are:\n1. `peterWeyl_clebschGordan_plaquette` (PeterWeyl.lean) — Peter-Weyl + CG + dual map (strengthened)\n2. `transferMatrixPositivity_axiom` (ReflectionPositivity.lean:1446) — **TARGET to close**\n3. `os_reconstruction_theorem` (OSAxioms.lean)\n4. `continuum_limit_exists` (ContinuumLimit.lean) — the open math core\n5. `mass_gap_axiom` (MassGap.lean) — THE CONJECTURE, do not remove\n6. `characterOrthogonality` (PositiveDefinite.lean:819) — Schur orthogonality\n\n## Closure plan progress (from docs/transfer_matrix_positivity_design.md)\n\nThe plan is the operator-theoretic T = B*·B argument. Four steps:\n\n- **Step (a): Separable decomposition of interface Boltzmann factor — COMPLETE.** `plaquette_product_separable_decomp` (PeterWeyl.lean:1110) proved, 0 sorries, 0 custom axioms. Shows ∏_p exp(c·Re Tr(g₁g₂g₃⁻¹g₄⁻¹)) = ∑_w F(w)·∏_l χ_{w(l)}(g_l) with F(w) ≥ 0.\n\n- **Step (b): Change of variables in transfer-matrix integral — COMPLETE.** `transferMatrix_change_of_variables` (TransferMatrix.lean:1994) proved, 0 sorries, 0 custom axioms. Shows `transferMatrixCorrect = transferMatrixReflected` via `reflectLinkVariable_measurePreserving_between` + `integral_map`. Key supporting lemmas all proved: `reflectToPosInterface_involution`, `reflectPosToNeg_reflectNegToPos`, `reflect_extendToFullConfig_posInterface`, `transferMatrix_integrand_change_of_variables`. Definitions: `reflectPosToNeg`, `reflectNegToPos`, `sigmaInterface`, `transferMatrixReflected`.\n\n- **Step (c): Use CG with dual representations + character orthogonality — NOT STARTED.** This is the next step. Goal: use `charProduct_mixed_finset_decomp'` and `charProduct_mixed_link_separable_decomp` (both proved in PeterWeyl.lean) together with `characterOrthogonality` (axiom) to evaluate the integrals and obtain ∑_w a_w · |Fourier coefficient|² ≥ 0.\n\n- **Step (d): Conclude T = B*·B and ⟨g, Tg⟩ = ‖Bg‖² ≥ 0 — NOT STARTED.** Assemble steps (a)-(c) to close `transferMatrixPositivity_axiom`.\n\n## Key files and locations\n\n- `src/lean/YangMills/Proofs/ReflectionPositivity.lean:1446` — the axiom `transferMatrixPositivity_axiom` (the target)\n- `src/lean/YangMills/Proofs/ReflectionPositivity.lean:1461` — `gibbsExpectationPeriodic_reflection_positive` (uses the axiom at line 1546)\n- `src/lean/YangMills/Proofs/TransferMatrix.lean` — transfer matrix definitions/lemmas (2973 lines). Key: `transferMatrixCorrect` (1213), `transferMatrixReflected` (1975), `transferMatrix_change_of_variables` (1994), `integral_G_thetaG_eq_inner_g_Tg` (proved, links ∫G·G(θU) to ⟨g,Tg⟩)\n- `src/lean/YangMills/Proofs/PeterWeyl.lean` — Peter-Weyl axiom + CG lemmas. Key: `plaquette_product_separable_decomp` (1110), `charProduct_mixed_finset_decomp'`, `charProduct_mixed_link_separable_decomp`\n- `src/lean/YangMills/Proofs/PositiveDefinite.lean:819` — `characterOrthogonality` axiom\n- `src/lean/YangMills/Proofs/PositiveDefiniteIntegral.lean:1009` — `character_expansion_positivity` (abstract scaffold; documented as NOT directly applicable to lattice case due to 3 obstructions — see gap_analysis.md lines 300-400)\n- `docs/transfer_matrix_positivity_design.md` — full design doc for the closure plan\n- `docs/gap_analysis.md` — full analysis, esp. lines 374-535 on why the operator-theoretic T=B*B approach is needed\n\n## The mathematical situation (read carefully)\n\nThe naive `character_expansion_positivity` approach does NOT directly apply (3 obstructions documented in gap_analysis.md:300-400): (1) θ⁻⁰ depends on both x and y, (2) pushforward of μ⁻ is singular, (3) σ reflection on interface time-like links gives χ(g)² not |χ(g)|². The correct approach is operator-theoretic: show T = B*·B via the character expansion, then ⟨g,Tg⟩ = ‖Bg‖² ≥ 0.\n\nThe key difficulty (design doc §4): for interface time-like links, reflection inverts the link (g↦g⁻¹), and χ(g⁻¹)=conj(χ(g))=χ_{dual}(g). The product χ_s(g)·conj(χ_t(g)) is a matrix coefficient of ρ_s⊗ρ_t*, decomposable via CG (with dual reps) into ∑_w N^w χ_w(g) with N^w ≥ 0. The dual map (added to the axiom) converts conj(χ) to χ_{dual}, enabling CG.\n\n## What to do next\n\n**Start step (c).** The natural first action is to study how `plaquette_product_separable_decomp` (step a) plugs into the reflected transfer matrix `transferMatrixReflected` (step b output), and where `characterOrthogonality` enters to evaluate the link integrals as |Fourier coefficients|². \n\nBefore writing code, re-read:\n1. `docs/transfer_matrix_positivity_design.md` §3 Step (c) and §4 (the σ reflection difficulty)\n2. `TransferMatrix.lean:1975-2059` (`transferMatrixReflected` def + `transferMatrix_change_of_variables`)\n3. `PeterWeyl.lean:1110-1326` (`plaquette_product_separable_decomp`)\n4. `PositiveDefinite.lean:819-828` (`characterOrthogonality` axiom statement)\n5. `PositiveDefiniteIntegral.lean:1009-1141` (`character_expansion_positivity` — the abstract scaffold, for the measure-theory techniques even though it doesn't apply directly)\n\nThe most likely path: define an operator B from the separable decomposition, show the reflected transfer matrix kernel equals B*·B's kernel, then ⟨g,Tg⟩=‖Bg‖²≥0. This is substantial formalization work. Consider the \"derived axiom\" intermediate approach (design doc §5): axiomatize the separable decomposition as a consequence of Peter-Weyl, prove positivity from it (pure measure theory + character orthogonality, removes transferMatrixPositivity_axiom → count stays 6), then prove the derived axiom from peterWeyl_clebschGordan_plaquette (count → 5). This decomposes the problem into cleaner pieces.\n\n## Conventions to follow\n\n- Every proof must be verified with `#print axioms` (only propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound allowed — no custom axioms, no sorry).\n- Update README.md \"What is actually proved\" / \"Known incomplete\" sections AND Overview.lean in the SAME session as any proof-state change.\n- Never describe the top-level Millennium Prize theorem as proved while mass_gap_axiom remains.\n- Keep `lake build` clean after every step. Build with: `lake build > tmp_build_full.log 2>&1` then check `findstr /I \"error sorry Build completed\" tmp_build_full.log`.\n- The README has a \"Keeping this README honest\" section — follow its discipline.\n\n## Session management\n\nCall `name_session` first. Check `project_task_list` (item 9 \"Close transferMatrixPositivity_axiom...\" is in_progress and tracks steps c,d). Use `todo_list` for this session's concrete steps. Update project_task_list when step (c) or (d) completes. Hand off before context exhausts (~75%).","timestamp":1785487250,"token_count":2276,"full_token_estimate":1480,"turn":0,"is_prune_marker":false}
