{"id":31,"role":"Tool","content":"path:C:\\github\\YangMills\\src\\lean\\YangMills\\Proofs\\TransferMatrix.lean\n-- 2973 lines, 109419 bytes --\n   1 | /-\n   2 | \n   3 | # Transfer Matrix: Corrected Approach\n   4 | \n   5 | \n   6 | \n   7 | This file provides definitions and lemmas toward a transfer matrix proof\n   8 | \n   9 | of the Osterwalder-Seiler reflection positivity for the periodic lattice.\n  10 | \n  11 | \n  12 | \n  13 | ## Mathematical Setup\n  14 | \n  15 | \n  16 | \n  17 | Let μ₀ = μ⁺ ⊗ μ⁻ ⊗ μ⁰ be the factorization of the product Haar measure on\n  18 | \n  19 | the finite periodic lattice into positive-time, negative-time, and interface\n  20 | \n  21 | links (via `measure_factorization'`).\n  22 | \n  23 | \n  24 | \n  25 | For an observable f depending only on links in the positive-time and interface\n  26 | \n  27 | regions (`dependsOnlyOnPosInterface N T L f`), define:\n  28 | \n  29 | \n  30 | \n  31 |     G(U) = f(U)·exp(-β·S_OS⁺(U))·exp(-β·S_OS_int(U)/2)\n  32 | \n  33 |     g(u) = f(u)·exp(-β·S_OS⁺(u)/2)   for u ∈ PosInterfaceConfig\n  34 | \n  35 | \n  36 | \n  37 | The reflection positivity lemma `gibbsExpectationPeriodic_reflection_positive`\n  38 | \n  39 | reduces to proving:\n  40 | \n  41 | \n  42 | \n  43 |     ∫ G(U)·G(θU) dμ₀(U) ≥ 0\n  44 | \n  45 | \n  46 | \n  47 | ## The Correct Transfer Matrix\n  48 | \n  49 | \n  50 | \n  51 | Define the transfer matrix T acting on functions ψ : PosInterfaceConfig → ℝ by:\n  52 | \n  53 | \n  54 | \n  55 |     (T ψ)(U⁺,U⁰) = ∫ ψ(θ⁻⁰(U⁻,U⁰))\n  56 | \n  57 |                      · exp(-β·(S_OS⁻(U⁻)+S_OS_int(U⁺,U⁻,U⁰))/2)\n  58 | \n  59 |                      dμ⁻(U⁻)\n  60 | \n  61 | \n  62 | \n  63 | where θ⁻⁰(U⁻,U⁰) is the restriction of θ(merge(U⁻,U⁰)) to positive+interface\n  64 | \n  65 | sites (i.e., reflecting the negative links to the positive side).\n  66 | \n  67 | \n  68 | \n  69 | ## Key Identity\n  70 | \n  71 | \n  72 | \n  73 |     ∫ G(U)·G(θU) dμ₀(U) = ∫_{PosInt} g(u)·(T g)(u) dμ⁺⁰(u)\n  74 | \n  75 | \n  76 | \n  77 | This holds because:\n  78 | \n  79 | 1. G(U)·G(θU) = g(U⁺,U⁰)·g(θ⁻⁰(U⁻,U⁰))\n  80 | \n  81 |                 · exp(-β·(S_OS⁻(U⁻)+S_OS_int(U⁺,U⁻,U⁰))/2)\n  82 | \n  83 | 2. The factorization μ₀ ≅ μ⁺ × μ⁻ × μ⁰ turns the LHS into an integral\n  84 | \n  85 |    over U⁺,U⁻,U⁰ of this expression.\n  86 | \n  87 | 3. Integrating out U⁻ gives (T g)(U⁺,U⁰) by definition.\n  88 | \n  89 | \n  90 | \n  91 | ## Positivity\n  92 | \n  93 | \n  94 | \n  95 | The operator T is POSITIVE because its integral kernel is a positive-definite\n  96 | \n  97 | function on (SU(N)ⁿ × SU(N)ⁿ). This follows from the Peter-Weyl theorem on\n  98 | \n  99 | SU(N) (Osterwalder-Seiler 1979, Theorem 3.1). Therefore ⟨g, T·g⟩ ≥ 0.\n 100 | \n 101 | \n 102 | \n 103 | ## Previous (Incorrect) Approach\n 104 | \n 105 | \n 106 | \n 107 | A previous version of this file defined a different transfer matrix that acted\n 108 | \n 109 | trivially (as a multiplication operator) because it did not apply the reflection\n 110 | \n 111 | θ⁻⁰ in the kernel.  This made the identity `transferMatrix_identity` false for\n 112 | \n 113 | general f.  The current approach corrects this by applying the reflection.\n 114 | \n 115 | \n 116 | \n 117 | ## References\n 118 | \n 119 | \n 120 | \n 121 | - K. Osterwalder, E. Seiler, \"Gauge Field Theories on a Lattice\"\n 122 | \n 123 |   (Ann. Phys. 110, 1978, pp 440–471), §3.\n 124 | \n 125 | - J. Glimm, A. Jaffe, \"Quantum Physics\" (2nd ed.), §6.1.\n 126 | \n 127 | - M. Lüscher, \"Some analytic results concerning the mass spectrum\n 128 | \n 129 |   of Yang-Mills gauge theories on a torus\" (1983)\n 130 | \n 131 | - M. Salmhofer, \"Construction of a Higgs field\" (thesis, 1990).\n 132 | \n 133 | -/\n 134 | \n 135 | \n 136 | \n 137 | import YangMills.Proofs.ReflectionPositivity\n 138 | \n 139 | import Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.MeasureSpaceDef\n 140 | \n 141 | import Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Constructions.Pi\n 142 | \n 143 | import Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Exp\n 144 | \n 145 | import Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.Haar.Basic\n 146 | \n 147 | import Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.Prod\n 148 | \n 149 | \n 150 | \n 151 | open Set\n 152 | \n 153 | open Matrix\n 154 | \n 155 | open scoped BigOperators\n 156 | \n 157 | open MeasureTheory\n 158 | \n 159 | \n 160 | \n 161 | namespace YangMills\n 162 | \n 163 | namespace Lattice\n 164 | \n 165 | \n 166 | \n 167 | section TransferMatrix\n 168 | \n 169 | \n 170 | \n 171 | variable (N T L : ℕ) [NeZero T] [NeZero L] (hT : Odd T) (β : ℝ)\n 172 | \n 173 | \n 174 | \n 175 | lemma measurable_reflectLinkVariable (N : ℕ) (T L : ℕ) [NeZero T] [NeZero L] :\n 176 | \n 177 |     Measurable (reflectLinkVariable N : LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L) → LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L)) := by\n 178 | \n 179 |   -- Use measurable_comap_iff to reduce to the value map:\n 180 | \n 181 |   -- reflectLinkVariable N is measurable into the comap space iff its value map is measurable\n 182 | \n 183 |   -- into the product space.\n 184 | \n 185 |   refine (measurable_comap_iff (g := fun (U' : LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L)) => U'.value)).mpr ?_\n 186 | \n 187 |   rw [measurable_pi_iff]\n 188 | \n 189 |   intro n\n 190 | \n 191 |   rw [measurable_pi_iff]\n 192 | \n 193 |   intro μ\n 194 | \n 195 |   simp [reflectLinkVariable]\n 196 | \n 197 |   by_cases hμ : μ = 0\n 198 | \n 199 |   · subst hμ\n 200 | \n 201 |     -- Need to show Measurable (λ U => (U.value (ReflectSite.reflectSite n) 0)⁻¹)\n 202 | \n 203 |     have h_val : Measurable (λ (U : LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L)) =>\n 204 | \n 205 |       U.value (ReflectSite.reflectSite n) 0) := by\n 206 | \n 207 |       -- The map U ↦ U.value is measurable from the comap definition\n 208 | \n 209 |       have h_value_map : Measurable (fun (U : LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L)) => U.value) :=\n 210 | \n 211 |         comap_measurable (fun (U : LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L)) => U.value)\n 212 | \n 213 |       -- Compose with coordinate projections\n 214 | \n 215 |       have h_at_n : Measurable (λ (f : PeriodicSite T L → Fin 4 → SU N) => f (ReflectSite.reflectSite n)) :=\n 216 | \n 217 |         measurable_pi_apply (ReflectSite.reflectSite n)\n 218 | \n 219 |       have h_at_n_0 : Measurable (λ (f : Fin 4 → SU N) => f 0) := measurable_pi_apply (0 : Fin 4)\n 220 | \n 221 |       exact h_at_n_0.comp (h_at_n.comp h_value_map)\n 222 | \n 223 |     -- Inversion is continuous, hence measurable\n 224 | \n 225 |     have h_inv : Measurable (λ (g : SU N) => g⁻¹) := (Continuous.inv continuous_id).measurable\n 226 | \n 227 |     exact h_inv.comp h_val\n 228 | \n 229 |   · -- μ ≠ 0, so U.value (θ n) μ (no inverse)\n 230 | \n 231 |     have h_val : Measurable (λ (U : LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L)) =>\n 232 | \n 233 |       U.value (ReflectSite.reflectSite n) μ) := by\n 234 | \n 235 |       have h_value_map : Measurable (fun (U : LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L)) => U.value) :=\n 236 | \n 237 |         comap_measurable (fun (U : LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L)) => U.value)\n 238 | \n 239 |       have h_at_n : Measurable (λ (f : PeriodicSite T L → Fin 4 → SU N) => f (ReflectSite.reflectSite n)) :=\n 240 | \n 241 |         measurable_pi_apply (ReflectSite.reflectSite n)\n 242 | \n 243 |       have h_at_n_μ : Measurable (λ (f : Fin 4 → SU N) => f μ) := measurable_pi_apply μ\n 244 | \n 245 |       exact h_at_n_μ.comp (h_at_n.comp h_value_map)\n 246 | \n 247 |     simpa [hμ] using h_val\n 248 | \n 249 | \n 250 | \n 251 | \n 252 | \n 253 | /-- The set of links at positive-time sites. -/\n 254 | \n 255 | noncomputable def positiveLinks : Finset (PeriodicSite T L × Fin 4) :=\n 256 | \n 257 |   (positiveSites T L).product (Finset.univ : Finset (Fin 4))\n 258 | \n 259 | \n 260 | \n 261 | /-- The set of links at negative-time sites. -/\n 262 | \n 263 | noncomputable def negativeLinks : Finset (PeriodicSite T L × Fin 4) :=\n 264 | \n 265 |   (negativeSites T L).product (Finset.univ : Finset (Fin 4))\n 266 | \n 267 | \n 268 | \n 269 | /-- The set of links at interface sites. -/\n 270 | \n 271 | noncomputable def interfaceLinks : Finset (PeriodicSite T L × Fin 4) :=\n 272 | \n 273 |   (interfaceSites T L).product (Finset.univ : Finset (Fin 4))\n 274 | \n 275 | \n 276 | \n 277 | lemma linkPartition_disjoint_union :\n 278 | \n 279 |     positiveLinks T L ∪ negativeLinks T L ∪ interfaceLinks T L =\n 280 | \n 281 |     (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L × Fin 4)) := by\n 282 | \n 283 |   ext ⟨n, μ⟩; simp [positiveLinks, negativeLinks, interfaceLinks, positiveSites,\n 284 | \n 285 |     negativeSites, interfaceSites]\n 286 | \n 287 |   by_cases hpos : signedTime T n.time > 0\n 288 | \n 289 |   · simp [hpos]\n 290 | \n 291 |   · by_cases hneg : signedTime T n.time < 0\n 292 | \n 293 |     · simp [hpos, hneg]\n 294 | \n 295 |     · have hzero : signedTime T n.time = 0 := by\n 296 | \n 297 |         have hle : signedTime T n.time ≤ 0 := by linarith\n 298 | \n 299 |         have hge : signedTime T n.time ≥ 0 := by linarith\n 300 | \n 301 |         linarith\n 302 | \n 303 |       simp [hpos, hneg, hzero]\n 304 | \n 305 | \n 306 | \n 307 | lemma linkPartition_disjoint :\n 308 | \n 309 |     Disjoint (positiveLinks T L) (negativeLinks T L) ∧\n 310 | \n 311 |     Disjoint (positiveLinks T L) (interfaceLinks T L) ∧\n 312 | \n 313 |     Disjoint (negativeLinks T L) (interfaceLinks T L) := by\n 314 | \n 315 |   have h_pos_neg_sites : Disjoint (positiveSites T L) (negativeSites T L) := by\n 316 | \n 317 |     unfold positiveSites negativeSites\n 318 | \n 319 |     rw [Finset.disjoint_filter]\n 320 | \n 321 |     intro n hn hpos hneg\n 322 | \n 323 |     linarith\n 324 | \n 325 |   have h_pos_int_sites : Disjoint (positiveSites T L) (interfaceSites T L) := by\n 326 | \n 327 |     unfold positiveSites interfaceSites\n 328 | \n 329 |     rw [Finset.disjoint_filter]\n 330 | \n 331 |     intro n hn hpos hzero\n 332 | \n 333 |     linarith\n 334 | \n 335 |   have h_neg_int_sites : Disjoint (negativeSites T L) (interfaceSites T L) := by\n 336 | \n 337 |     unfold negativeSites interfaceSites\n 338 | \n 339 |     rw [Finset.disjoint_filter]\n 340 | \n 341 |     intro n hn hneg hzero\n 342 | \n 343 |     linarith\n 344 | \n 345 |   have h_pos_neg_links : Disjoint (positiveLinks T L) (negativeLinks T L) := by\n 346 | \n 347 |     unfold positiveLinks negativeLinks\n 348 | \n 349 |     simpa using (Finset.disjoint_product (s := positiveSites T L) (t := Finset.univ)\n 350 | \n 351 |       (s' := negativeSites T L) (t' := Finset.univ)).mpr (Or.inl h_pos_neg_sites)\n 352 | \n 353 |   have h_pos_int_links : Disjoint (positiveLinks T L) (interfaceLinks T L) := by\n 354 | \n 355 |     unfold positiveLinks interfaceLinks\n 356 | \n 357 |     simpa using (Finset.disjoint_product (s := positiveSites T L) (t := Finset.univ)\n 358 | \n 359 |       (s' := interfaceSites T L) (t' := Finset.univ)).mpr (Or.inl h_pos_int_sites)\n 360 | \n 361 |   have h_neg_int_links : Disjoint (negativeLinks T L) (interfaceLinks T L) := by\n 362 | \n 363 |     unfold negativeLinks interfaceLinks\n 364 | \n 365 |     simpa using (Finset.disjoint_product (s := negativeSites T L) (t := Finset.univ)\n 366 | \n 367 |       (s' := interfaceSites T L) (t' := Finset.univ)).mpr (Or.inl h_neg_int_sites)\n 368 | \n 369 |   exact ⟨h_pos_neg_links, h_pos_int_links, h_neg_int_links⟩\n 370 | \n 371 | \n 372 | \n 373 | /-- The union of positive, negative, and interface sites covers all sites. -/\n 374 | \n 375 | lemma sites_cover (T L : ℕ) [NeZero T] [NeZero L] :\n 376 | \n 377 |     (positiveSites T L) ∪ (negativeSites T L) ∪ (interfaceSites T L) = Finset.univ := by\n 378 | \n 379 |   ext n; simp [positiveSites, negativeSites, interfaceSites]\n 380 | \n 381 |   by_cases hpos : signedTime T n.time > 0\n 382 | \n 383 |   · simp [hpos]\n 384 | \n 385 |   · by_cases hneg : signedTime T n.time < 0\n 386 | \n 387 |     · simp [hpos, hneg]\n 388 | \n 389 |     · have hzero : signedTime T n.time = 0 := by\n 390 | \n 391 |         have hle : signedTime T n.time ≤ 0 := by linarith\n 392 | \n 393 |         have hge : signedTime T n.time ≥ 0 := by linarith\n 394 | \n 395 |         linarith\n 396 | \n 397 |       simp [hpos, hneg, hzero]\n 398 | \n 399 | \n 400 | \n 401 | /-- Haar measure on the positive links. -/\n 402 | \n 403 | noncomputable def haarMeasurePositive : Measure (FiniteLinkConfig N (PeriodicSite T L) (positiveSites T L)) :=\n 404 | \n 405 |   productHaarMeasure N (PeriodicSite T L) (positiveSites T L)\n 406 | \n 407 | \n 408 | \n 409 | /-- Haar measure on the negative links. -/\n 410 | \n 411 | noncomputable def haarMeasureNegative : Measure (FiniteLinkConfig N (PeriodicSite T L) (negativeSites T L)) :=\n 412 | \n 413 |   productHaarMeasure N (PeriodicSite T L) (negativeSites T L)\n 414 | \n 415 | \n 416 | \n 417 | /-- Haar measure on the interface links. -/\n 418 | \n 419 | noncomputable def haarMeasureInterface : Measure (FiniteLinkConfig N (PeriodicSite T L) (interfaceSites T L)) :=\n 420 | \n 421 |   productHaarMeasure N (PeriodicSite T L) (interfaceSites T L)\n 422 | \n 423 | \n 424 | \n 425 | /-- A helper equivalence: `FiniteLinkIndex Λ (s₁ ∪ s₂) ≃ FiniteLinkIndex Λ s₁ ⊕ FiniteLinkIndex Λ s₂`\n 426 | \n 427 | for disjoint s₁, s₂. -/\n 428 | \n 429 | noncomputable def finiteLinkIndexUnionSum {Λ : Type} [DecidableEq Λ] {s₁ s₂ : Finset Λ}\n 430 | \n 431 |     (h : Disjoint s₁ s₂) : FiniteLinkIndex Λ (s₁ ∪ s₂) ≃ FiniteLinkIndex Λ s₁ ⊕ FiniteLinkIndex Λ s₂ where\n 432 | \n 433 |   toFun := λ x =>\n 434 | \n 435 |     if h₁ : x.1.1 ∈ s₁ then\n 436 | \n 437 |       Sum.inl ⟨(x.1.1, x.1.2), h₁⟩\n 438 | \n 439 |     else\n 440 | \n 441 |       have h₂ : x.1.1 ∈ s₂ := by\n 442 | \n 443 |         rcases Finset.mem_union.mp x.2 with (h₁' | h₂')\n 444 | \n 445 |         · exact (h₁ h₁').elim\n 446 | \n 447 |         · exact h₂'\n 448 | \n 449 |       Sum.inr ⟨(x.1.1, x.1.2), h₂⟩\n 450 | \n 451 |   invFun :=