{"id":34,"role":"Tool","content":"Search results (5):\n\n1. [https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/BF01614090]\n   Construction of a selfadjoint, strictly positive transfer matrix for ...\n   It is shown that physical positivity holds in Wilson's lattice gauge theories, i.e. transition probabilities between gauge invariant states are non-negative and the quantum mechanical Hamiltonian has real eigenvalues only.\n\n2. [https://projecteuclid.org/journals/communications-in-mathematical-physics/volume-113/issue-3/General-proof-of-Osterwalder-Schrader-positivity-for-the-Wilson-action/cmp/1104160284.pdf]\n   PDF General Proof of Osterwalder-Schrader Positivity for the Wilson Action\n   Luscher [3] and independently Osterwalder and Seiler [4] have addressed the problem in two different ways. Luscher starting from the Wilson action builds up a Hubert space as a Fock space derived from equal time fields and explicitly constructs a transfer matrix [5] which he proves to be positive definite, in this context Osterwalder-Schrader positivity is proved for gauge invariant operators ...\n\n3. [https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/0003491678900398]\n   Gauge field theories on a lattice - ScienceDirect\n   This implies the existence of a positive self-adjoint transfer matrix. We then prove existence and analyticity of the infinite volume limit of strongly coupled Yang-Mills theories on the lattice and we verify Wilson's confinement bound. Finally we present a rigorous treatment of the Higgs mechanism in lattice gauge theories.\n\n4. [https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/0550321384902700]\n   Definition and general properties of the transfer matrix in continuum ...\n   When operators of dimension 6 are added to the standard Wilson action in lattice gauge theories, physical positivity is lost in general. We show that a transfer matrix can nevertheless be defined. Its properties are, however, unusual: complex eigenvalues may occur (leading to damped oscillatory behaviour of correlation functions), and there are always contributions in the spectral ...\n\n5. [https://projecteuclid.org/journals/communications-in-mathematical-physics/volume-54/issue-3/Construction-of-a-selfadjoint-strictly-positive-transfermatrix-for-euclidean-lattice/cmp/1103900872.full]\n   Construction of a selfadjoint, strictly positive transfer matrix for ...\n   1977 Construction of a selfadjoint, strictly positive transfer matrix for euclidean lattice gauge theories M. Lüscher\n\n","timestamp":1785491164,"token_count":616,"tool_call_id":"b28f05fb-594f-45e3-a715-cb33430a6c5f","full_token_estimate":514,"tool_meta":{"tool_name":"web_search","file_path":null,"old_text":"Lüscher \"transfer matrix\" positivity lattice gauge theory proof character expansion Osterwalder Seiler","new_text":null,"exit_code":null,"line_count":null,"byte_count":2450,"is_error":false,"duration_ms":1097,"edit_line":null},"turn":20,"is_prune_marker":false}
