n\nEach term ∫ χ_μ(U) · χ_ν(θU) · exp(-β·S_W(U)) dμ₀(U) can be evaluated using the character expansion and character orthogonality. The result is a sum of CG coefficients, which are non-negative.\n\nBut the sum ∑_{μ, ν} c_μ · c_ν · [non-negative terms] is NOT necessarily non-negative, because c_μ and c_ν can have different signs.\n\nWait, but f is REAL-valued. So c_μ are the Fourier coefficients of a real-valued function. For a real-valued function, the Fourier coefficients satisfy c_{dual(μ)} = conj(c_μ). But since f is real, c_μ are real (if the characters are real) or come in conjugate pairs.\n\nHmm, this is getting complicated. Let me think about it differently.\n\nActually, I think the key insight is that for the reflection positivity, we need f to be supported on positive+interface links (dependsOnlyOnPosInterface). This means f only depends on U⁺ and u⁰, not on U⁻. So the character expansion of f is over U⁺ and u⁰ links only.\n\nThe integral is:\n```\n∫ f(U) · f(θU) · exp(-β·S_W(U)) dμ₀(U)\n```\n\nwhere f depends on U⁺ and u⁰, and θU reflects U to θU (with U⁺ → U⁻, u⁰ → σ(u⁰), U⁻ → U⁺).\n\nSo f(θU) depends on U⁻ and σ(u⁰). The integral over U⁻ of f(θU) · [character expansion of exp(-β·S_W) restricted to U⁻ links] gives a function of U⁺ and u⁰.\n\nThis is exactly the transfer matrix construction. The integral over U⁻ gives (Tf)(U⁺, u⁰), and the full integral is ∫ f(U⁺, u⁰) · (Tf)(U⁺, u⁰) dμ⁺⁰(U⁺, u⁰).\n\nSo we're back to the transfer matrix positivity problem.\n\nOK, I've spent an enormous amount of context on this analysis. Let me just write the analysis document and move on. I'll document the key findings:\n\n1. The direct character_expansion_positivity approach fails due to obstruction 3.\n2. The OS proof uses T = B*·B, but the exact mechanism is subtle.\n3. The decomposition T = M·T₀·M doesn't help because T₀ has the same obstruction.\n4. The key gap is understanding how the OS proof resolves obstruction 3.\n5. The proposed approach is the \"derived axiom\" approach, where the derived axiom captures the key identity.\n\nLet me write the analysis and update the docs. I'll also check the build status.\n\nActually, I realize I should be more productive. Instead of just writing analysis, let me try to make concrete progress on the formalization. Even if I can't prove the full result, I can:\n\n1. Define the \"core\" transfer matrix T₀ (without the S⁺ factors).\n2. Show T = M·T₀·M (the decomposition).\n3. Show that if T₀ is positive, then T is positive.\n4. Define a derived axiom that T₀ is positive.\n5. Prove transferMatrixPositivity_axiom from the derived axiom.\n\nThis would be concrete progress, even if the derived axiom is not yet proved.\n\nLet me start by checking the build status and then working on the formalization.\n\nActually, I realize I'm at 60% context usage. Let me be efficient and focus on the most productive tasks.\n\nLet me check the build status first, then write the analysis and start the formalization.","turn":25,"is_prune_marker":false}
