{"id":50,"role":"Assistant","content":"","timestamp":1785493226,"token_count":0,"tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"old_text\":\"**Key insight for future sessions**: the `character_expansion_positivity`\\nlemma, while a valuable abstract result, is NOT the right scaffold for the\\nlattice case.  The correct approach is the operator-theoretic `T = B* B`\\nargument, which requires CG and the full plaquette combinatorics.  The\\nabstract lemma's requirement that `θ : Y → X` be a function of `y` only (and\\nmeasure-preserving to the FULL measure on `X`) is fundamentally incompatible\\nwith the lattice setup's shared interface structure and the `σ` reflection on\\ninterface time-like links.\",\"path\":\"docs/gap_analysis.md\",\"new_text\":\"**Key insight for future sessions**: the `character_expansion_positivity`\\nlemma, while a valuable abstract result, is NOT the right scaffold for the\\nlattice case.  The correct approach is the operator-theoretic `T = B* B`\\nargument, which requires CG and the full plaquette combinatorics.  The\\nabstract lemma's requirement that `θ : Y → X` be a function of `y` only (and\\nmeasure-preserving to the FULL measure on `X`) is fundamentally incompatible\\nwith the lattice setup's shared interface structure and the `σ` reflection on\\ninterface time-like links.\\n\\n### ✅ Step (c) analysis complete (2026-07-31 session): L² expansion obstruction\\n\\nA detailed analysis of step (c) was performed.  **The key finding is a\\nfundamental obstruction**: closing `transferMatrixPositivity_axiom` from the\\ncurrent axioms alone is NOT possible.  The obstruction is the **L² expansion\\n(Peter-Weyl completeness)**, which is not provided by the current axioms.\\n\\n**The obstruction in detail.**  After steps (a)–(b), the integral to show ≥ 0 is:\\n\\n    I = ∫_u ∫_{V⁺} f(u) · f(V⁺, σ(u⁰)) · K(u, V⁺) dμ⁺(V⁺) dμ⁺⁰(u)\\n\\nwhere K(u, V⁺) = exp(-β·(S⁺(u) + S⁺(V⁺, σ(u⁰)) + S_int(U⁺, u⁰, reflect(V⁺)))).\\nThe character expansion of K (step a) gives K = ∑_w F(w) · Φ_w(U⁺) · Ψ_w(u⁰) · Ξ_w(V⁺)\\nwith F(w) ≥ 0.  By reflection symmetry, Ξ_w = Φ_w.  So:\\n\\n    I = ∑_w F(w) · ∫_{u⁰} Ψ_w(u⁰) · A_w(u⁰) · A_w(σ(u⁰)) dμ⁰(u⁰)\\n\\nwhere A_w(u⁰) = ∫_{u⁺} f(u⁺, u⁰) · Φ_w(u⁺) dμ⁺(u⁺).  This is\\n⟨A_w · Ψ_w, A_w ∘ σ⟩_{L²(μ⁰)}, which is **obstruction 3**: NOT necessarily\\nnon-negative, because the σ reflection on interface time-like links gives\\nA_w(u⁰) · A_w(σ(u⁰)) instead of |A_w(u⁰)|².\\n\\n**Why the current axioms are insufficient.**  To evaluate the u⁰ integral using\\ncharacter orthogonality, one must expand A_w(u⁰) in the character/matrix-element\\nbasis (the L² expansion).  But:\\n- `peterWeyl_clebschGordan_plaquette` provides the character expansion of the\\n  **Boltzmann factor** (a specific function), NOT the L² expansion of\\n  **arbitrary** functions.\\n- `characterOrthogonality` provides Schur orthogonality of characters\\n  (∫ χ_λ · conj(χ_μ) = δ_{λμ}), which is an **orthogonality** statement, not a\\n  **completeness** statement.\\n\\nThe L² expansion is a completeness statement: the matrix elements\\n{ρ_λ(g)_{ij}} span ALL of L²(G).  Since A_w(u⁰) depends on the arbitrary test\\nfunction f, it is NOT a class function in general, so it cannot be expanded in\\ncharacters alone — the full matrix element basis is needed.\\n\\n**Proposed path forward.**  Strengthen `peterWeyl_clebschGordan_plaquette` to\\ninclude the L² expansion (Peter-Weyl theorem: matrix elements form an\\northonormal basis of L²(G)) and Schur orthogonality of matrix elements\\n(∫ ρ_λ(g)_{ij} · conj(ρ_μ(g)_{kl}) dμ = δ_{λμ} δ_{ik} δ_{jl} / dim(λ)).\\nThis keeps the axiom count at 6 (strengthening, not adding) and provides the\\nkey ingredient to close `transferMatrixPositivity_axiom` (count → 5).\\n\\nSee `docs/transfer_matrix_positivity_design.md` §5a for the full analysis.\"}","name":"patch_file"},"id":"8492f87b-e411-4910-80ad-e67888cc1701","type":"function"}],"full_token_estimate":793,"turn":35,"is_prune_marker":false}
{"id":51,"role":"Tool","content":"Patched C:\\github\\YangMills\\docs\\gap_analysis.md via exact (46178 -> 48777 bytes, line 528)","timestamp":1785493226,"token_count":32,"tool_call_id":"8492f87b-e411-4910-80ad-e67888cc1701","full_token_estimate":39,"tool_meta":{"tool_name":"patch_file","file_path":"docs/gap_analysis.md","old_text":"**Key insight for future sessions**: the `character_expansion_positivity`\nlemma, while a valuable abstract result, is NOT the right scaffold for the\nlattice case.  The correct approach is the operator-theoretic `T = B* B`\nargument, which requires CG and the full plaquette combinatorics.  The\nabstract lemma's requirement that `θ : Y → X` be a function of `y` only (and\nmeasure-preserving to the FULL measure on `X`) is fundamentally incompatible\nwith the lattice setup's shared interface structure and the `σ` reflection on\ninterface time-like links.","new_text":"**Key insight for future sessions**: the `character_expansion_positivity`\nlemma, while a valuable abstract result, is NOT the right scaffold for the\nlattice case.  The correct approach is the operator-theoretic `T = B* B`\nargument, which requires CG and the full plaquette combinatorics.  The\nabstract lemma's requirement that `θ : Y → X` be a function of `y` only (and\nmeasure-preserving to the FULL measure on `X`) is fundamentally incompatible\nwith the lattice setup's shared interface structure and the `σ` reflection on\ninterface time-like links.\n\n### ✅ Step (c) analysis complete (2026-07-31 session): L² expansion obstruction\n\nA detailed analysis of step (c) was performed.  **The key finding is a\nfundamental obstruction**: closing `transferMatrixPositivity_axiom` from the\ncurrent axioms alone is NOT possible.  The obstruction is the **L² expansion\n(Peter-Weyl completeness)**, which is not provided by the current axioms.\n\n**The obstruction in detail.**  After steps (a)–(b), the integral to show ≥ 0 is:\n\n    I = ∫_u ∫_{V⁺} f(u) · f(V⁺, σ(u⁰)) · K(u, V⁺) dμ⁺(V⁺) dμ⁺⁰(u)\n\nwhere K(u, V⁺) = exp(-β·(S⁺(u) + S⁺(V⁺, σ(u⁰)) + S_int(U⁺, u⁰, reflect(V⁺)))).\nThe character expansion of K (step a) gives K = ∑_w F(w) · Φ_w(U⁺) · Ψ_w(u⁰) · Ξ_w(V⁺)\nwith F(w) ≥ 0.  By reflection symmetry, Ξ_w = Φ_w.  So:\n\n    I = ∑_w F(w) · ∫_{u⁰} Ψ_w(u⁰) · A_w(u⁰) · A_w(σ(u⁰)) dμ⁰(u⁰)\n\nwhere A_w(u⁰) = ∫_{u⁺} f(u⁺, u⁰) · Φ_w(u⁺) dμ⁺(u⁺).  This is\n⟨A_w · Ψ_w, A_w ∘ σ⟩_{L²(μ⁰)}, which is **obstruction 3**: NOT necessarily\nnon-negative, because the σ reflection on interface time-like links gives\nA_w(u⁰) · A_w(σ(u⁰)) instead of |A_w(u⁰)|².\n\n**Why the current axioms are insufficient.**  To evaluate the u⁰ integral using\ncharacter orthogonality, one must expand A_w(u⁰) in the character/matrix-element\nbasis (the L² expansion).  But:\n- `peterWeyl_clebschGordan_plaquette` provides the character expansion of the\n  **Boltzmann factor** (a specific function), NOT the L² expansion of\n  **arbitrary** functions.\n- `characterOrthogonality` provides Schur orthogonality of characters\n  (∫ χ_λ · conj(χ_μ) = δ_{λμ}), which is an **orthogonality** statement, not a\n  **completeness** statement.\n\nThe L² expansion is a completeness statement: the matrix elements\n{ρ_λ(g)_{ij}} span ALL of L²(G).  Since A_w(u⁰) depends on the arbitrary test\nfunction f, it is NOT a class function in general, so it cannot be expanded in\ncharacters alone — the full matrix element basis is needed.\n\n**Proposed path forward.**  Strengthen `peterWeyl_clebschGordan_plaquette` to\ninclude the L² expansion (Peter-Weyl theorem: matrix elements form an\northonormal basis of L²(G)) and Schur orthogonality of matrix elements\n(∫ ρ_λ(g)_{ij} · conj(ρ_μ(g)_{kl}) dμ = δ_{λμ} δ_{ik} δ_{jl} / dim(λ)).\nThis keeps the axiom count at 6 (strengthening, not adding) and provides the\nkey ingredient to close `transferMatrixPositivity_axiom` (count → 5).\n\nSee `docs/transfer_matrix_positivity_design.md` §5a for the full analysis.","exit_code":null,"line_count":null,"byte_count":null,"is_error":false,"duration_ms":0,"edit_line":528},"turn":35,"is_prune_marker":false}
