{"id":53,"role":"Tool","content":"C:\\github\\YangMills\\README.md\n-- 748 lines, 49206 bytes --\n 1 | # Yang-Mills Millennium Prize — Lean 4 Formalization\n 2 | \n 3 | A Lean 4 formalization effort around the mathematical foundations of quantum\n 4 | Yang-Mills theory, undertaken with the long-term goal of a formally verified\n 5 | proof of the Yang-Mills existence and mass gap conjecture (Clay Millennium\n 6 | Prize Problem).\n 7 | \n 8 | **Status as of this update: the Millennium Prize theorem is NOT proved.**\n 9 | The top-level statement currently depends on an axiom\n10 | (`mass_gap_axiom`) that is logically equivalent to the conjecture itself.\n11 | Any derivation from that axiom is circular and should not be read as\n12 | progress on the open problem. See \"Status of the Millennium Prize Theorem\"\n13 | below before reading anything else in this document.\n14 | \n15 | > **Maintenance note:** this README must be kept in sync with the actual\n16 | > Lean source on every session that touches the proof state (new lemmas,\n17 | > new axioms, new sorries, sorries closed, axioms removed). Do not let\n18 | > claims here drift ahead of — or behind — what `lake build` and\n19 | > `#print axioms` actually report. See \"Keeping this README honest\" at the\n20 | > bottom.\n21 | \n22 | ---\n23 | \n24 | ## Status of the Millennium Prize Theorem\n25 | \n26 | **Not proved.** The formalization currently rests on **six** axioms (not\n27 | four — `MassGapProof.lean`'s module docstring says \"four axioms\" and then\n28 | lists five; that docstring needs fixing too), one of which (`mass_gap_axiom`)\n29 | directly encodes the conjecture being proved. Any theorem chain that\n30 | terminates in this axiom is not a proof of anything new — it is a\n\n... 718 more line(s) below (use offset=31 to continue reading)","timestamp":1785493324,"token_count":440,"tool_call_id":"05fc6310-463c-440c-9472-003edfc917a5","full_token_estimate":391,"tool_meta":{"tool_name":"read_file","file_path":"REA