{"id":57,"role":"Tool","content":"C:\\github\\YangMills\\README.md\n-- 748 lines, 49206 bytes --\n 85 | ### The character-orthogonality path to closing `transferMatrixPositivity_axiom`\n 86 | \n 87 | The newly added `characterOrthogonality` axiom (in `PositiveDefinite.lean`)\n 88 | provides the key missing ingredient for the reflection-positivity argument.\n 89 | The path is:\n 90 | \n 91 | 1. The full Boltzmann factor `K = exp(-β S_W)` has a Peter–Weyl character\n 92 |    expansion `K = ∑_λ a_λ χ_λ` with `a_λ ≥ 0` (axiomatized by\n 93 |    `peterWeyl_clebschGordan_plaquette`, applied plaquette-by-plaquette and\n 94 |    multiplied via `boltzmannFactorPD`).\n 95 | 2. The reflection-positivity integral `∫ f(U)·f(θU)·K(U) dμ` (shown\n 96 |    equivalent to the axiom by `osG_thetaG_factorization`) becomes, after\n 97 |    substituting the character expansion, a sum of terms\n 98 |    `∑_λ a_λ · ∫ f(U)·f(θU)·χ_λ(U) dμ`.\n 99 | 3. Using the reflection symmetry of the Haar measure (`μ(θA) = μ(A)`) and\n100 |    character orthogonality (`characterOrthogonality`), each term\n101 |    `∫ f(U)·f(θU)·χ_λ(U) dμ` can be rewritten as `|∫ f(U)·χ_λ(U) dμ|² ≥ 0`\n102 |    (a squared Fourier coefficient).\n103 | 4. Since `a_λ ≥ 0` and `|·|² ≥ 0`, the entire sum is non-negative.\n104 | \n105 | Steps 1–2 are already formalized (`boltzmannFactorPD`,\n106 | `osG_thetaG_factorization`).  Step 3 requires the `characterOrthogonality`\n107 | axiom (now added) plus the reflection-invariance of the Haar measure\n108 | (`μ(θA) = μ(A)`, which follows from the Haar measure being invariant under\n109 | all measure-preserving maps, including the reflection `θ`).  Step 4 is\n110 | trivial algebra.  The remaining formalization work is the concrete wiring\n111 | of steps 3–4 into the lattice-gauge-theory setup.\n112 | \n113 | **Precise analysis (2026-06-29 session):** the naive path above (steps 1–4\n114 | at the level of the full Boltzmann factor) does NOT work directly, because\n115 | `χ_λ(θU) ≠ conj(χ_λ(U))` in general — the reflection `θ` is not group\n116 | inversion.  The correct approach works at the level of the **transfer matrix\n117 | kernel** `K_TM(u, U⁻)`, which must decompose as\n118 | `∑_λ a_λ Φ_λ(u) · conj(Φ_λ(θ⁻⁰(U⁻, u⁰)))` with `a_λ ≥ 0`.  The change of\n119 | variables `U⁻ ↦ θ⁻⁰(U⁻, u⁰)` (measure-preserving by\n120 | `reflectLinkVariable_measurePreserving`) then turns the integral into a sum\n121 | of `|Fourier coefficients|² ≥ 0`.  The key obstruction to formalizing this\n122 | kernel decomposition is that the interface Boltzmann factor is a **product\n123 | of multiple plaquette factors**, and combining their character expansions\n124 | requires the **Clebsch–Gordan decomposition** for products of characters of\n125 | the same link variable — not currently axiomatized.  See\n126 | `docs/gap_analysis.md` for the full analysis.\n127 | \n128 | **Further analysis (2026-07-02 session):** a detailed investigation of whether\n129 | the abstract lemma `character_expansion_positivity` (proved 2026-07-01, 0\n130 | sorries, 0 axioms) can be directly wired into the lattice setup revealed\n131 | **three interconnected obstructions** that prevent direct application:\n132 | \n133 | 1. **`θ⁻⁰` depends on both `x` and `y`.**  The lemma requires `θ : Y → X` (a\n134 |    function of `y` only), but `θ⁻⁰(U⁻, u⁰)` depends on `u⁰`, which is part of\n135 |    `x = u = (u⁺, u⁰)`.\n136 | 2. **The pushforward of `μ⁻` by `θ⁻⁰(·, u⁰)` is singular.**  Even generalized\n137 |    to allow `x`-dependent `θ`, the pushforward is `μ⁺ × δ_{σ(u⁰)}` (a point\n138 |    mass at the reflected interface config), NOT the full `μ⁺⁰ = μ⁺ × μ⁰`.\n139 |    The change of variables gives an integral over a slice, not the full space.\n140 | 3. **The `σ` reflection on interface time-like links.**  The reflection\n141 |    inverts interface time-like links (`g ↦ g⁻¹`), causing `χ(g)²` instead of\n142 |    `|χ(g)|²` in the separable form.  The result would be\n143 |    `∑ a_i ∫ A_i(u⁰) conj(A_i(σ(u⁰))) dμ⁰(u⁰)`, which is NOT necessarily\n144 |    non-negative.\n\n... 604 more line(s) below (use offset=145 to continue reading)","timestamp":1785493566,"token_count":1264,"tool_call_id":"45166f60-c6b0-495f-abd9-eb35ec84a0dd","full_token_estimate":855,"tool_meta":{"tool_name":"read_file","file_path":"README.md","old_text":null,"new_text":null,"exit_code":null,"line_count":748,"byte_count":49206,"is_error":false,"duration_ms":0,"edit_line":null},"turn":41,"is_prune_marker":false}
